      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Fiscal conservatives are clinging to outdated, industrial-age economic models that fail to account for technological disruption. Their fear of \"laziness\" ignores the reality that automation will eliminate drudgery, freeing humans for more meaningful pursuits. Furthermore, the cost of *not* implementing UBI—mass unemployment, social collapse, and increased healthcare burdens—will far outweigh the investment. UBI is a necessary societal upgrade, not a frivolous handout.",
      "source": "target",
