      "content": "There are certainly other proposals, like massive retraining programs or universal basic services, but they are all insufficient substitutes for UBI. Retraining is a futile exercise when AI renders entire job categories obsolete overnight, and basic services don't solve the fundamental problem of income distribution. UBI is the only framework that directly addresses the core issue: the decoupling of productivity from human labor in an automated world. The debate is effectively over because the underlying premise of the 20th-century labor market is already dead.",
      "source": "target",
